1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
A symbol table maps every declared name to what the compiler knows about it.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
The key is the name; the value is the attributes.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Two operations, insert and lookup, and nothing else is essential.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Created in lexical analysis, read by every phase after it.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,000
A table of declarations is not a table of data.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Eight names arrive in the order the compiler meets them.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Before appending, the insert scans for a duplicate.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
The first insert scans nothing; the eighth scans seven.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Twenty-eight comparisons in total, which is eight times seven over two.

10
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,000
A lookup in the worst case walks the whole list.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,000
A search tree compares once per level, so the height is the cost.

12
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Inserted alphabetically, every name hangs off the right of the last.

13
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:18,000
That tree costs twenty-eight comparisons, exactly the list.

14
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Inserted median-first, the tree stays shallow: height three.

15
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Thirteen comparisons against twenty-eight, from the order alone.

16
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:36,000
A hash table turns the name into a bucket number.

17
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:42,000
main and count both land in bucket three.

18
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Eight entries, six buckets used, longest chain two.

19
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Occupation density is entries over buckets: eight elevenths.

20
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:00,000
A lookup probes one bucket and compares against its chain.

21
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Each organisation has one quantity that decides its cost.

22
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Building: twenty-eight against thirteen against eight inserts.

23
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Looking up: the list scans, the tree descends, the bucket is computed.

24
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Every cost is a claim about an assumption.

25
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Which is why the answer names the structure, the quantity and the case.

26
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,000
This program declares count twice, in two different blocks.

27
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Two declarations mean two entries, not one.

28
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Inside the block, count means the inner declaration.

29
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:54,000
The closing brace ends the inner meaning.

30
00:02:54,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Six entries, five reachable names.

31
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Entering a block pushes a table; leaving it pops one.

32
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:12,000
A lookup starts at the top and walks outward.

33
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:18,000
count costs one probe; total costs three.

34
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:24,000
So a lookup costs the depth, not one operation.

35
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:30,000
The pop is what brings the outer binding back.

36
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:36,000
A single table can do the same job, with duplicate keys.

37
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:42,000
The first match in the bucket is the innermost binding.

38
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:48,000
A log records what each scope added, so the exit can undo it.

39
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:54,000
So lookup is constant and the exit is constant on average.

40
00:03:54,000 --> 00:04:00,000
The stack is easier to build; the single table is faster to read.

41
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
The global table holds total and main.

42
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:12,000
main's own table holds count and rate, and not main.

43
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:18,000
The inner block adds a second count and code.

44
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Which is why a later function cannot be called without a prototype.

45
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Six entries, three tables, one shadowed name.

46
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Shape one: which statement about the table is false.

47
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Shape two: how many entries, or which binding.

48
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Shape three: which organisation is faster, and why.

49
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Three shapes, three pictures, one procedure.

50
00:04:54,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Draw the structure, name the quantity, state the case.

